        "subject": "LU-18302 tests: commit client records in recovery-small 134",
        "message": "LU-18302 tests: commit client records in recovery-small 134\n\ntest_134 remounts the clients and then fails mds1 a few seconds\nlater. The new clients' last_rcvd records are written in a\ntransaction that is not synced, so when a HARD failover powers the\nMDS off before the next journal commit, the MDTs restart with the\nrecords of the old mounts. Every client is then refused as a new\nclient during recovery and evicted when it ends, and the rm and mv\nfail with EIO or ESHUTDOWN. SOFT failover unmounts the targets,\nwhich commits the records, so only the failover sessions fail.\n\nSync the MDTs after the remount so the records are on disk before\nthe race starts. Create the test directories on MDT0000, so that\nthe race always runs on the MDT that \"fail mds1\" takes down.\n\nFixes: 58edec38160f (\"LU-11131 target: keep reply data bit set on failover\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial env=FAILURE_MODE=HARD,ONLY=134,ONLY_REPEAT=20   clientcount=3 mdtcount=1 mdscount=2 osscount=2 austeroptions=-R   failover=true iscsi=1 fstype=ldiskfs testlist=recovery-small\nTest-Parameters: env=FAILURE_MODE=HARD,ONLY=134,ONLY_REPEAT=10   clientcount=3 mdtcount=1 mdscount=2 osscount=2 austeroptions=-R   failover=true iscsi=1 fstype=zfs testlist=recovery-small\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I076dca3b0c709e245c9c1d17f0a0315c6dc1dbba\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master",
